is it anyway?"

1017
00:46:02,560 --> 00:46:04,663
I'm a sailor.
[Whimpers]

1018
00:46:04,697 --> 00:46:06,265
Will you help me?

1019
00:46:06,298 --> 00:46:09,300
Hmm?

1020
00:46:09,333 --> 00:46:12,170
What, what?
What?

1021
00:46:12,203 --> 00:46:15,440
Ohh. No!

1022
00:46:15,473 --> 00:46:17,342
No! Oh...

1023
00:46:19,945 --> 00:46:23,848
Michael Caine and Nancy kulp
are vampires.

1024
00:46:23,882 --> 00:46:25,617
Shoot, roommates!

1025
00:46:28,020 --> 00:46:30,722
David bowie,
from "the hunger."

1026
00:46:31,657 --> 00:46:33,958
He's all dewy.

1027
00:46:33,992 --> 00:46:34,960
Dewy bowie.

1028
00:46:34,993 --> 00:46:39,097
I hate jetlag.

1029
00:46:39,130 --> 00:46:40,498
Boy, I really racked up

1030
00:46:40,532 --> 00:46:41,867
the frequent flier miles,
though.

1031
00:46:41,900 --> 00:46:43,702
Yeah, frequent dier miles!

1032
00:46:43,735 --> 00:46:44,703
[Laughter]

1033
00:46:44,737 --> 00:46:46,505
Jeez.
You're feeling better?

1034
00:46:46,538 --> 00:46:48,573
A little.

1035
00:46:48,607 --> 00:46:50,208
Kessler!

1036
00:46:50,242 --> 00:46:51,577
Ingrid!

1037
00:46:51,610 --> 00:46:52,978
In color!

1038
00:46:55,547 --> 00:46:58,417
She's kind of overdressed
for espionage.

1039
00:46:58,450 --> 00:47:01,987
Professor heracles.

1040
00:47:02,020 --> 00:47:03,722
[Grunts]

1041
00:47:03,755 --> 00:47:07,292
She had to sit next
to the stinky guy.

1042
00:47:07,325 --> 00:47:10,128
Eww, uck.

1043
00:47:10,162 --> 00:47:12,230
Oh, I can't watch this.

1044
00:47:12,263 --> 00:47:15,833
I mean,
I can't see this.

1045
00:47:15,867 --> 00:47:18,803
It's kind of like a metallica
video, but slower.

1046
00:47:18,837 --> 00:47:21,373
Come on, what is this,
kirlian photography?

1047
00:47:21,407 --> 00:47:23,775
Yeah, moe, Larry, and kirlian
photography.

1048
00:47:23,808 --> 00:47:25,843
Yeah, heh.

1049
00:47:25,877 --> 00:47:28,347
Jeez, and I thought "city of
hope" was an underlit movie.

1050
00:47:28,380 --> 00:47:31,148
Uck.

1051
00:47:31,182 --> 00:47:32,650
Ugh.

1052
00:47:32,683 --> 00:47:35,053
They've been candied!

1053
00:47:35,087 --> 00:47:36,722
- Candide?
- Candide.

1054
00:47:36,755 --> 00:47:38,090
Where are we?

1055
00:47:38,123 --> 00:47:40,558
You're one step away
from never working again.

1056
00:47:40,592 --> 00:47:45,463
Anatolia...
Near the bosphorus.

1057
00:47:45,497 --> 00:47:50,002
They've turned us
into warhols!

1058
00:47:50,035 --> 00:47:51,370
It's incredible.

1059
00:47:51,403 --> 00:47:52,503
What?

1060
00:47:52,537 --> 00:47:53,805
Who were those people?

1061
00:47:53,838 --> 00:47:55,707
[Imitating thurston howell]
Who are these people?

1062
00:47:55,740 --> 00:48:01,580
...kidnapped by the men
of fu manchu.

1063
00:48:01,613 --> 00:48:03,715
Fu man--

1064
00:48:03,748 --> 00:48:05,417
manchu,
spit it out, honey.

1065
00:48:05,450 --> 00:48:11,155
I can't move.
I feel I'm paralyzed.

1066
00:48:11,188 --> 00:48:14,292
You'll be all right
in a few minutes.

1067
00:48:14,325 --> 00:48:18,530
They used my crystals
against you.

1068
00:48:18,563 --> 00:48:21,367
The first color movie
that needs to be colorized.

1069
00:48:21,400 --> 00:48:24,502
But in a small dose.

1070
00:48:24,535 --> 00:48:25,837
[Groaning]

1071
00:48:25,870 --> 00:48:27,205
Professor!

1072
00:48:27,238 --> 00:48:28,307
Look, you're overtired.

1073
00:48:28,340 --> 00:48:30,542
We'll talk to you later.

1074
00:48:30,575 --> 00:48:33,845
Ah.

1075
00:48:33,878 --> 00:48:35,447
She could use
a good Clay pack.

1076
00:48:35,480 --> 00:48:36,748
- Mm-hmm.
- Yeah, yeah.

1077
00:48:36,782 --> 00:48:39,117
Spores.
Ew.

1078
00:48:39,150 --> 00:48:42,120
Come on.

1079
00:48:42,153 --> 00:48:46,157
Meanwhile,
in downtown duluth.

1080
00:48:46,190 --> 00:48:47,325
That's not funny.

1081
00:48:47,358 --> 00:48:49,093
I went to Istanbul,
and all I got

1082
00:48:49,127 --> 00:48:50,828
was this lousy Fez, huh?

1083
00:48:50,862 --> 00:48:52,130
- Heh heh.
- That's funny.

1084
00:48:52,163 --> 00:48:54,465
Hey, take a long walk
off that thing.

1085
00:48:54,498 --> 00:48:56,435
Yeah.

1086
00:48:59,403 --> 00:49:01,238
Hi, we're the boatniks.

1087
00:49:01,272 --> 00:49:03,708
[Chuckles]

1088
00:49:07,345 --> 00:49:08,313
Inspector Hammond?

1089
00:49:08,347 --> 00:49:10,615
You inspect her, I'm busy.

1090
00:49:10,648 --> 00:49:12,050
An honor, sir.

1091
00:49:12,083 --> 00:49:14,385
But I'm afraid
that I have bad news.

1092
00:49:14,418 --> 00:49:15,787
What is the bad news,
inspector?

1093
00:49:15,820 --> 00:49:17,055
My hat.

1094
00:49:17,088 --> 00:49:18,957
The bandits, sir,
who attacked at the castle

1095
00:49:18,990 --> 00:49:21,360
were Omar pasha's men.

1096
00:49:21,393 --> 00:49:22,593
Omar pasha?

1097
00:49:22,627 --> 00:49:24,562
He controls the opium trade.

1098
00:49:24,595 --> 00:49:25,563
- The perfume?
- Opium?!

1099
00:49:25,597 --> 00:49:28,467
An informer called melnick

1100
00:49:28,500 --> 00:49:30,802
appeared this morning,
killed.

1101
00:49:30,835 --> 00:49:32,870
Bzz!
Tell me again, please.

1102
00:49:32,903 --> 00:49:34,773
I need your help,
please.

1103
00:49:34,807 --> 00:49:38,743
...to Omar pasha's coffee shop.

1104
00:49:38,777 --> 00:49:41,747
- ♪ Omar pasha ♪
- [chuckles]

1105
00:49:41,780 --> 00:49:44,415
I should have
listened to him.

1106
00:49:44,448 --> 00:49:45,417
Why?

1107
00:49:45,450 --> 00:49:48,887
Omar pasha has vanished.

1108
00:49:48,920 --> 00:49:51,957
Meanwhile in--
aw, forget it.

1109
00:49:51,990 --> 00:49:55,460
...that he has gone to anatolia
to rescue the girl Lisa

1110
00:49:55,493 --> 00:49:58,063
and is camped opposite
the castle on the other side...

1111
00:49:58,097 --> 00:50:01,265
Looks like two seals
waterskiing, doesn't it?

1112
00:50:01,298 --> 00:50:02,900
- Mm-hmm.
- Kinda?

1113
00:50:02,933 --> 00:50:04,102
No.

1114
00:50:04,135 --> 00:50:06,372
♪ Allah ♪

1115
00:50:06,405 --> 00:50:09,107
♪ oh, lord, it's hard
to be a mole ♪

1116
00:50:09,140 --> 00:50:10,108
[Chuckles]

1117
00:50:10,142 --> 00:50:12,310
Ah.

1118
00:50:12,343 --> 00:50:13,878
♪ Allah ♪

1119
00:50:13,912 --> 00:50:15,347
Uh-oh.

1120
00:50:18,250 --> 00:50:20,085
Hey, it's the grand wizard
himself.

1121
00:50:20,118 --> 00:50:22,320
- What a boring--
- wow.

1122
00:50:22,353 --> 00:50:24,088
[Chanting]

1123
00:50:24,122 --> 00:50:25,090
Ooh!

1124
00:50:25,123 --> 00:50:27,325
Agh!

1125
00:50:27,358 --> 00:50:28,427
- Come on!
- Thank you.

1126
00:50:28,460 --> 00:50:29,795
Thank you,
next show at 10:00.

1127
00:50:29,828 --> 00:50:32,097
Thank you very much.

1128
00:50:32,130 --> 00:50:34,833
Hey, uh, don't
step in the guy, heh.

1129
00:50:34,867 --> 00:50:38,137
Ugh.

1130
00:50:38,170 --> 00:50:40,572
- All is clear, master.
- Come on.

1131
00:50:40,605 --> 00:50:44,608
Oh, jeez, I thought shriners
helped people.

1132
00:50:44,642 --> 00:50:46,945
Rock the kasbah, dude.

1133
00:50:46,978 --> 00:50:49,480
Sharia don't like it.

1134
00:50:49,513 --> 00:50:51,215
Ah, wouldn't it be great
if we knew

1135
00:50:51,248 --> 00:50:52,683
who they were,
where they are,

1136
00:50:52,717 --> 00:50:53,685
or what they were doing?

1137
00:50:53,718 --> 00:50:55,120
Yeah, pretty much.

1138
00:50:55,153 --> 00:50:57,955
Well, he looks like a century 21
salesman.

1139
00:50:57,988 --> 00:50:58,957
Yeah, with that--

1140
00:50:58,990 --> 00:51:01,358
Gandhi's back,
and he's stuffed.

1141
00:51:01,392 --> 00:51:03,328
Fu manchu.

1142
00:51:03,362 --> 00:51:04,328
♪♪

1143
00:51:04,362 --> 00:51:06,532
Bring forth
the two prisoners.

1144
00:51:06,565 --> 00:51:09,033
Dr. Kessler
and Dr. Ingrid coch.

1145
00:51:09,067 --> 00:51:10,168
Yes, father.

1146
00:51:10,202 --> 00:51:11,703
The guards are
bringing them.

1147
00:51:11,737 --> 00:51:13,872
Oh, look, it's the original
hand-hammered wok.

1148
00:51:13,905 --> 00:51:15,607
Yeah, looks like stainless steel
from here.

1149
00:51:15,640 --> 00:51:16,942
Ohh... yeah, you're right.

1150
00:51:20,212 --> 00:51:21,312
Love me.

1151
00:51:21,345 --> 00:51:23,148
I have brought you here
to save

1152
00:51:23,182 --> 00:51:25,983
the life of someone
whose knowledge I require

1153
00:51:26,017 --> 00:51:28,153
as a thirsty
man needs water.

1154
00:51:28,187 --> 00:51:30,155
Tonight,
on "you asked for it"...

1155
00:51:30,188 --> 00:51:31,322
Clear water.

1156
00:51:31,355 --> 00:51:33,958
Crystal blue persuasion.

1157
00:51:33,992 --> 00:51:35,860
Ah, cripes, this again.

1158
00:51:35,893 --> 00:51:43,302
The name of the person to whom
I refer is professor heracles.

1159
00:51:43,335 --> 00:51:46,572
Uh, we're underwhelmed.

1160
00:51:49,908 --> 00:51:51,477
You know, Burt young
has looked worse.

1161
00:51:51,510 --> 00:51:53,010
Mm-hmm.

1162
00:51:56,615 --> 00:51:58,950
Well, he's Burt young,
all right.

1163
00:51:58,983 --> 00:52:01,587
- He is dying.
- Oh, professor.

1164
00:52:01,620 --> 00:52:03,322
You will use your skill,
doctor.

1165
00:52:03,355 --> 00:52:04,488
You will make him live.

1166
00:52:04,522 --> 00:52:06,658
Damn it, fu, I'm a surgeon,
not a doctor!

1167
00:52:06,692 --> 00:52:08,927
I am not a miracle worker.

1168
00:52:08,960 --> 00:52:13,698
Besides, you took everything
away except my hands.

1169
00:52:13,732 --> 00:52:15,700
On the contrary,
Dr. Kessler.

1170
00:52:15,733 --> 00:52:18,203
Et cetera, et cetera,
et cetera.

1171
00:52:18,237 --> 00:52:24,008
You will find everything here
that you require.

1172
00:52:24,042 --> 00:52:27,378
Let's see what's
behind door number one.

1173
00:52:27,412 --> 00:52:29,547
Ooh.

1174
00:52:33,352 --> 00:52:35,220
Here, I have
everything you need.

1175
00:52:35,253 --> 00:52:37,822
I threw in the hairy
naked man just for kicks.

1176
00:52:37,855 --> 00:52:38,923
Nice touch.

1177
00:52:40,758 --> 00:52:42,160
What's wrong with that man?

1178
00:52:42,193 --> 00:52:43,328
Nothing at all.

1179
00:52:43,362 --> 00:52:44,897
There is nothing wrong
with him, doctor.

1180
00:52:44,930 --> 00:52:47,065
He is in perfect
physical condition.

1181
00:52:47,098 --> 00:52:48,098
I'll say.

1182
00:52:48,132 --> 00:52:50,035
And, unlike
professor heracles,

1183
00:52:50,068 --> 00:52:51,970
his heart is sound
as a bell.

1184
00:52:52,003 --> 00:52:53,272
Bong!

1185
00:52:53,305 --> 00:52:56,207
Do you not agree, doctor,
that professor heracles

1186
00:52:56,240 --> 00:52:58,877
should have
that splendid heart?

1187
00:52:58,910 --> 00:53:01,212
Ah, if it comes
with that beefy chest!

1188
00:53:01,245 --> 00:53:03,282
- Ooh...
- Mm!

1189
00:53:03,315 --> 00:53:06,050
But that man is not dead
or dying.

1190
00:53:06,083 --> 00:53:07,785
He's only mostly dead!

1191
00:53:07,818 --> 00:53:10,988
He will die for the sake
of science.

1192
00:53:11,022 --> 00:53:13,925
And for your sake, also.

1193
00:53:13,958 --> 00:53:16,160
I need heracles
to complete my plans.

1194
00:53:16,193 --> 00:53:19,130
I need him alive--
conscious, coherent.

1195
00:53:19,163 --> 00:53:21,600
I wish this movie were conscious
and coherent!

1196
00:53:21,633 --> 00:53:24,768
[Laughing]

1197
00:53:24,802 --> 00:53:27,138
And if I refuse?

1198
00:53:27,172 --> 00:53:28,773
I hadn't thought of that.

1199
00:53:28,807 --> 00:53:29,942
Gosh, he's clever.

1200
00:53:29,975 --> 00:53:31,577
Then Dr. Ingrid coch

1201
00:53:31,610 --> 00:53:33,778
will die an extremely painful
death.

1202
00:53:33,812 --> 00:53:34,778
Oh good.

1203
00:53:34,812 --> 00:53:35,780
No!

1204
00:53:35,813 --> 00:53:38,583
Uh, fresh ground pepper
with that?

1205
00:53:38,617 --> 00:53:40,418
Mmm.

1206
00:53:40,452 --> 00:53:43,588
The choice is yours,
Dr. Kessler.

1207
00:53:43,622 --> 00:53:45,123
Well?

1208
00:53:45,157 --> 00:53:47,725
In order to convince you,

1209
00:53:47,758 --> 00:53:50,162
I shall arrange
a demonstration.

1210
00:53:53,230 --> 00:53:54,265
No!

1211
00:53:54,298 --> 00:53:56,835
No! No!

1212
00:53:56,868 --> 00:53:58,503
♪♪

1213
00:53:58,537 --> 00:53:59,770
What's going on?

1214
00:53:59,803 --> 00:54:03,775
Glen Manning,
get off that dam!

1215
00:54:03,808 --> 00:54:05,077
"Bridge on the river kwai."

1216
00:54:05,110 --> 00:54:06,745
Looks like it, doesn't it?

1217
00:54:08,413 --> 00:54:10,348
Biggest crack by a dam site.

1218
00:54:10,382 --> 00:54:11,717
- Doh!
- Ohh.

1219
00:54:11,750 --> 00:54:12,883
Right there.

1220
00:54:12,917 --> 00:54:13,918
Hey, there's a little
Dutch boy

1221
00:54:13,952 --> 00:54:15,053
putting his finger in there.

1222
00:54:15,087 --> 00:54:17,088
Where?

1223
00:54:17,122 --> 00:54:19,757
Run!
Run for your lives!

1224
00:54:19,790 --> 00:54:20,892
Run, men!

1225
00:54:20,925 --> 00:54:22,760
The plot's starting
to make sense!

1226
00:54:22,793 --> 00:54:23,828
Run!

1227
00:54:23,862 --> 00:54:26,330
- Run!
- Run!

1228
00:54:29,233 --> 00:54:31,035
Oh, this dam scene.

1229
00:54:31,068 --> 00:54:34,372
Hey, don't forget
to punch out!

1230
00:54:34,405 --> 00:54:37,675
You know, um...

1231
00:54:37,708 --> 00:54:39,577
I suddenly have to go
to the bathroom.

1232
00:54:39,610 --> 00:54:40,778
- Really?
- Yep.

1233
00:54:40,812 --> 00:54:42,247
Why, I wonder?

1234
00:54:42,280 --> 00:54:44,482
Funniest thing.

1235
00:54:47,018 --> 00:54:48,185
- Ooh.
- You know, they might need

1236
00:54:48,218 --> 00:54:49,920
some Thompson's water seal
up there.

1237
00:54:49,953 --> 00:54:52,090
- Yeah, I think so,
to hold it back.

1238
00:54:52,123 --> 00:54:53,492
Don't worry, men.

1239
00:54:53,525 --> 00:54:57,195
It's the Egyptians
who are gonna get us.

1240
00:54:57,228 --> 00:54:58,697
Pharaoh and the gang.

1241
00:54:58,730 --> 00:55:01,198
Tsk, tsk, tsk, tsk.

1242
00:55:02,433 --> 00:55:03,435
Ooh.

1243
00:55:03,468 --> 00:55:05,337
[All cheering]

1244
00:55:05,370 --> 00:55:07,772
We're getting off early!
Whoo!

1245
00:55:07,805 --> 00:55:10,175
Free day!

1246
00:55:10,208 --> 00:55:11,977
"Force 10 from navarone."

1247
00:55:12,010 --> 00:55:12,977
Mm-hmm.

1248
00:55:13,010 --> 00:55:14,945
Oh, quit groveling.

1249
00:55:14,978 --> 00:55:15,913
Graveling?

1250
00:55:15,947 --> 00:55:18,048
[Man screaming]

1251
00:55:20,118 --> 00:55:22,720
Uh-huh.
Yep, yep.

1252
00:55:22,753 --> 00:55:23,822
Uh, you know,
cutting it faster

1253
00:55:23,855 --> 00:55:25,657
doesn't make it
any more exciting.

1254
00:55:27,958 --> 00:55:30,262
[All sigh]

1255
00:55:30,295 --> 00:55:31,562
Ohh, that's a relief.

1256
00:55:31,595 --> 00:55:33,297
I didn't think that dam
would ever break.

1257
00:55:33,330 --> 00:55:36,567
Huh-uh.

